--- body ---
## Context

`skills/external-peer-review/peer_review.py:87` reads `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` from
`os.environ`, falling back to walking parent directories for a `.env` that
assigns it. Both paths depend on the credential being ambient or on a file that
is not the keystore.

Child of 0942. The pattern to copy is `skills/reviewers/reviewers.sh`
(ticket 0393): locate the provider file defining the variable, extract that one
variable in an `env -i` subshell, never print / log / argv the value.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Resolves from `~/.config/keys/` at point of use; env still wins if set
- [ ] The `.env`-walking fallback is removed, not merely deprioritized
- [ ] Fails loud and named when the credential cannot be resolved -- never a
      silent no-op (see feedback_gaze_external_seats_fail_open)
- [ ] Fake-sentinel test, never a real key; asserts against a child process
- [ ] `make check` passes
